{
	"contract": "_shared/metrics/data/studio_ngrams.json",
	"description": "The saved Ergopti Studio « My typing » read every driver keeps in its keystats cache folder: one header line (the contract's snapshot format, a space, then the store stamp the read was made at), then the payload JSON. Windows (KLR_StudioSnapshotRead, KLR_StudioSnapshotWrite) and macOS and Linux (metrics/engine/view/studio_ngrams.lua, decode_snapshot and encode_snapshot) replay these vectors. format and schema must equal the contract's, so a change of either fails every driver until the vectors follow. A read vector with a stamp is accepted with that stamp and its body as the payload; one without is refused (fail fast: a corrupt or mismatched saved read is never shown). A write vector without text is refused; with text, it is the file written.",
	"format": "ergopti-studio-ngrams 1",
	"schema": 2,
	"reads": [
		{
			"id": "accepted",
			"text": "ergopti-studio-ngrams 1 rev-7\n{\"schema\":2,\"source\":\"keystats\",\"chars\":{\"a\":1},\"total\":1}",
			"stamp": "rev-7"
		},
		{
			"id": "accepted_schema_last",
			"text": "ergopti-studio-ngrams 1 4f2a\n{\"source\":\"keystats\",\"chars\":{\"e\":2},\"schema\":2}",
